WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.830
You might want to take
a step back there, Captain.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.203
I'm sorry.
I know I'm staring a lot.
Huge fan. Huge fan.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.772
Been following your career
for quite a while now.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:16.743
Visual tower,
this is Shuttle Marmota
approaching docking bay four.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.746
Closing the blast shields.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:88% position:13%
-<i> Shuttle Marmota,
  you're clear to dock.</i> 
- Yeah. Copy you.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.086
Truth be told,
we couldn't afford
to show that anyway,

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.387
but, yeah,
don't get me wrong.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.389
I know exactly
where we're heading.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:33.760
Check it out.
We're gonna land in five--

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.231
( clanking, hissing )

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:42.235
Captain, we're here early.
I gotta say, it's an honor.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:46.071
I was thinking maybe
we could hang out or something?

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:48.941
Go get a coffee.
But, you know, beer's cool.

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:52.077
( alarm buzzing )

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.380
Welcome aboard
the Invincible II, Captain.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.482
Glad to have you here.
Took you long enough.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:59.252
But let me give you
the grand tour before we embark.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
- This is my pride and joy.
- No!

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.890
My baby.
Well, your baby, I guess, now.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:09.095
But I made her,
and a baby will always
remember her father.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.097
Computer:<i> Bio-scan.</i>

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.265
<i> Welcome aboard, Captain,
 and head engineer.</i>

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:16.435
<i> Prepare for sterilization.</i>

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.939
First stop, the warp core,
the heart and soul of the ship.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.740
Still not 100% sure
how it works,

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.611
but you don't need to know
how something works

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.312
in order to use it.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:33.219
And when we found it again,
it passed every safety test
with flying colors.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:91% position:9%
- It's not gonna be
  like last time. Oh, no.
- Aah! My eyes!

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.926
This time the Invincible
is finally gonna live up
to her name.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.762
But just in case,
I built in a special precaution.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:46.632
If anything goes wrong,
we can detonate these explosives

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.268
and separate the warp core
from the rest of the ship.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.603
( imitates explosion )

00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:54.440
I've yet to meet a problem
that can't be solved
with explosives.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.777
And speaking of explosives,
the main reactor!

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.645
It turns out you pretty much
need the power of a star

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.148
to tear open a wormhole,
so a star I built.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.883
Built like a tank, too.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:16.262
Captain. Burt.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yep.
- That's Burt.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.733
He makes sure that
the ship don't go boom.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:25.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Next up is Cryo. Oh, hey.
- Hey, Mark.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.473
The colonists are prepped,
stable, and ready for transit.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.642
Systems are working
at 110%, too,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.844
which is a little weird,
but overkill never hurts.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.445 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Trust me.
- Woman: Hello!

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:36.349
You do not want to be awake
when the warp core hits the gas.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.350
Woman:
I think I'm supposed
to be asleep,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.420
but I don't think I am.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.656 align:start size:66% position:34%
- CC.
- Asshat.

00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:47.527 align:start position:0%
Captain, all colonists
are prepped and stable.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.361 align:start position:0%
100,000 souls
ready for a new life.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Let's get them there safe.
- Oh, don't worry.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.065 align:start size:66% position:34%
before they know it,
they're gonna wake up

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:66% position:34%
to the sight
of a brand new planet

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start position:0%
with a fresh cup of coffee
in their hands.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.737 align:start size:91% position:9%
Why don't you give them
more windows to look through?

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.373 align:start position:0%
Well, maybe I will!

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:03.042
Maybe then someone might
appreciate the aesthetics.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:06.912
Besides, what could go wrong
with a crew like this?

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.881 align:start position:0%
ADS is good to go.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.217 align:start position:0%
Don't worry, Captain.
No asteroid's getting by me.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.718 align:start position:0%
You can count on that.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:16.555 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> ( PA chatter )</i> 
- ( overlapping chatter )

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.257
Computer:<i> Requesting
 additional personnel.</i>

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.759
Hey, watch it!

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.927
Oh, my God, I'm so--

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:27.133
Oh, no. Captain, I'm falling!
Catch me! Aah!

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.400
( bones crack )

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.269 align:start size:66% position:34%
Navigation is online,
Captain.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.137 align:start size:78% position:22%
Engines are looking good,
Captain.

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.273
Life support is online,
unless it's not,

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.576
and then we wouldn't know
until we passed out.

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.746
Seems fine.
Everything is accounted for.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.347
We're ready to see
our new home.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.616
All that's left now...

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:47.953
...is for you to say the word.

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:50.289 align:start size:66% position:34%
Try not to get them
too excited, Captain.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:75% position:25%
I know how your speeches
can get people riled up.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.800
( clears throat )

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.502
( coughing )

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.137
Computer:
<i> Warp core engaged.</i>

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.306
( alarm blaring )

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.408
<i> Wormhole opening
 in 30 seconds.</i>

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:12.144
<i> All personnel report
 to your assigned cryo-pod.</i>

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:13.780
Ah, it's all right, Captain.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:18.083
I'm sure you'll make a great
speech once we get there.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:21.620
( mumbling )

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.256
Oh, and I forgot to mention,
it's not a problem, of course,

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:28.861
but just before you go to sleep,
be absolutely sure, do not--

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:33.232
Computer:
<i> Wormhole opening
 in ten, nine, eight,</i>

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:38.137
<i> seven, six-- error.</i>

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:40.205
<i> Error, error, error,
 error, error, error, error.</i>

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.941
<i> Wormhole opening
 in three, two--</i>

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:44.810
Voice:
<i> A software update
 is available.</i>

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.680
<i> Would you like to restart
 to apply this update?</i>

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:54.520
<i> ( overlapping voices )</i>

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.624
<i> Don't give up.</i>

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.497
Voice:
<i> Software update complete.</i>

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.065
Computer:
<i> Good morning, Captain.</i>

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.500
<i> We are currently ERROR years
 into our journey.</i>

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.102
<i> Coffee is en route.</i>

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:15.341
<i> Current ship status
 is absolutely catastrophic.</i>

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:20.513
<i> Initializing emergency
 Wakey-Wakey Protocol.</i>

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:25.585
<i> ( alarms blaring )</i>

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.891 align:start size:91% position:9%
- ( explosion )
-<i> Reviving head engineer.</i>

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.063
( grunting )

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:39.865
Captain,
what the hell is-- aah!

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:42.668
<i> Hull breach detected.
 Sealing bulkhead.</i>

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.873
<i> Fire on the bridge.</i>

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:49.876
<i> Error.
 Life support systems failing.</i>

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:53.245
<i> Error. Automatic Fire
 Suppression System offline.</i>

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.915
<i> Error.
 Fail-safes offline.</i>

